    "narrative": "The offensive engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP relies heavily on **Tyler Soderstrom** (69.25) and **Corbin Carroll** (67.82) today, as both anchor the top end of our efficiency spectrum. **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits from a massive park-factor boost (+10%) facing Soriano, while **Corbin Carroll** remains our premier engine for stolen base production. Even against a left-handed starter in Prielipp, **Corbin Carroll**\u2019s projected upside is too high to ignore, especially given our focus on elite sprint speed to stay competitive in the scarcity-driven SB category. **Brice Turang** also earns a strong nod (61.57) batting third; he is the most efficient play in the middle infield, leveraging a favorable matchup against the left-handed P\u00e9rez.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s board involved **Cole Young** (41.98), who sat just outside the starting threshold. Despite a decent projection, **Cole Young** was edged out because of his platoon disadvantage against the left-handed Suarez and a lack of the explosive upside provided by **Kyle Karros** (49.03), who benefits from a significant +14% park factor boost despite his bottom-of-the-order slot. We are also tracking potential volatility for **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**, as their scores are currently based on projected lineup positions. Should either be slotted lower than anticipated against Gibson, their efficiency scores will slide further toward our floor, potentially forcing a defensive re-evaluation of the bench depth.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the heavy concentration of left-handed pitching we are facing today. **Gabriel Moreno** (56.05) and **Josh Naylor** (50.79) are both staring down unfavorable platoon matchups against Prielipp and Suarez, respectively. While **Josh Naylor** remains in the lineup due to his high base projection, his score has been tempered by both the park and the SP skill matchup. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Seiya Suzuki** (52.85) and **James Wood** (50.67); both are fighting through elite-level opposing arms, but their ability to generate value via high xwOBA and speed on the basepaths\u2014particularly with **James Wood**\u2019s elite speed profile\u2014keeps them in the mix over stagnant options like **Cole Young**.",
